>> title: Miso Ramen
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: pork, japanese, ramen, noodles, miso
>> counters: Ramen Shop
>> aka: miso ramen, 味噌ラーメン, Sapporo ramen, Sapporo miso ramen, miso-ramen, a bowl of miso, corn butter ramen
>> pairs-with: chintan-broth, miso-tare, ramen-noodles, chashu
>> servings: 1
>> time: 15 min

>> step: The broth is finished in a wok, so this one is cooked rather than assembled.
The one bowl on the board that is cooked rather than assembled — the broth is finished in a wok, and it goes to the table hotter than the other three.

>> step: fry the pork hard 3 min
Fry @ground pork{3%oz}(85 g) in @lard{1%Tbs}(15 g) in a #wok{} over high heat ~fry{3%min}, breaking it fine and letting it catch and brown rather than steam.

>> step: toss the sprouts and aromatics in, 1 min
Toss @bean sprouts{1%cup}(90 g), @cabbage{1%cup}(70 g; cut in squares), @garlic{1%clove}(grated) and @fresh ginger{1%tsp}(grated) into @&(~1)pork{} ~stirfry{1%min}, until the sprouts have gone glassy at the edges and are still crisp in the middle.

>> step: spoon the tare in, let it catch 30 sec
Stir @miso tare{3%Tbs}(55 g) into @&(~1)pork and vegetables{} and let it sit against the hot metal ~fry{30%sec}, until it smells toasted.

>> step: pour the broth in, boil 1 min, into the bowl
Pour @chintan broth{1 1/2%cups}(350 mL) into @&(~1)wok{}, bring it to a hard ~boil{1%min} while scraping the bottom clean, then tip the lot into a scalded #ramen bowl{}.

>> step: boil 3 min, drain, into the broth
Boil @ramen noodles{6%oz}(170 g; 3 mm thick and curly) in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L; hard-boiling, unsalted) ~boil{3%min}, drain them hard and lift them into @&(~1)miso broth{}.

>> step: top with corn and butter
Top @&(~1)bowl{} with @sweetcorn{1/4%cup}(40 g; warmed), @unsalted butter{1%Tbs}(15 g; one cold pat), @chāshū{2%slices}(warmed) and @scallion{1%stalk}(thinly sliced).
